# Firestore security rules — example (docs only)

> **Not deployed.** Copy into a Firebase project / emulator only after gates + `firebase/firestore-rules` PR.  
> Path: `users/{uid}/save/current` — see [`docs/en/FIREBASE_ADR.md`](../en/FIREBASE_ADR.md).

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    function isOwner(userId) {
      return request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }

    function hasSaveEnvelope() {
      return request.resource.data.keys().hasAll([
        'schemaVersion',
        'gameSaveVersion',
        'revision',
        'payloadChecksum',
        'payload'
      ])
      && request.resource.data.revision is int
      && request.resource.data.payloadChecksum is string;
    }

    match /users/{userId}/save/{docId} {
      allow read: if isOwner(userId) && docId == 'current';
      allow create, update: if isOwner(userId) && docId == 'current' && hasSaveEnvelope();
      allow delete: if isOwner(userId) && docId == 'current';
    }

    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
```

Tighten size limits and schemaVersion bounds in the real `firebase/firestore-rules` PR.

## Emulator test checklist (scaffold)

Run against Firebase Emulator Suite in `firebase/firestore-rules` PR:

| # | Case                                      | Expect        |
| - | ----------------------------------------- | ------------- |
| 1 | Signed-out read `users/u1/save/current`   | **deny**      |
| 2 | Signed-out write                          | **deny**      |
| 3 | Auth as `u1`, read/write own `current`    | **allow**     |
| 4 | Auth as `u1`, write `users/u2/...`        | **deny**      |
| 5 | Auth as `u1`, write doc id ≠ `current`    | **deny**      |
| 6 | Missing `revision` / `payloadChecksum`    | **deny**      |
| 7 | Oversized `payload` (limit TBD in PR)     | **deny**      |
| 8 | Unrelated collection path                 | **deny**      |

Commands (placeholder — pin versions in runtime PR):

```bash
firebase emulators:start --only firestore
# then rules unit tests (Jest/@firebase/rules-unit-testing or equivalent)
```
